# API rate limits

New routes under `/api` **must** register through [`server/rate-limit/api.ts`](server/rate-limit/api.ts) — not raw `app.post("/api/...")`.

```ts
import { api } from "../rate-limit/api.js";

api.post(app, "/api/example", { rate: "staffWrite" }, handler);
api.get(app, "/api/health", { rate: "exempt", reason: "health probe" }, handler);
```

## Policies

| Policy | Use for |
|---|---|
| `expensiveAi` | OpenRouter image generation |
| `expensiveCapture` | Cloudflare Browser Run / entry-preview enqueue |
| `staffWrite` | Default for staff mutating APIs (future) |
| `publicRead` | Public read APIs (future) |
| `auth` | Login / OAuth (future) |
| `exempt` | Deliberate opt-out — **requires `reason`** |

Limits are per-identity (+ global ceiling on expensive policies). Only **successful 2xx** responses consume quota.

Streaming handlers (e.g. generate-images NDJSON) must call `markRateLimitSuccess(res)` when a billable success completes, or `markRateLimitNoCharge(res)` on cancel/error.

Legacy `app.*` routes are grandfathered; run `npm run check:api-rate` to list offenders. New work uses `api.*`.

Store is in-memory per process (resets on restart). Redis can plug in later via `RateLimitStore`.
